  "helpBody": "The quickest help is at the store. You can also call or message us.",
  "faq1q": "How can I pay?",
  "faq1a": "By UPI, credit or debit card, net banking, or cash (at the store, or on delivery in town). You can also use Bajaj Finserv EMI or card EMI.",
  "faq2q": "How does Bajaj Finserv EMI work?",
  "faq2a": "Apply in the app and pay a small down payment. Visit the store with your Aadhaar, PAN and bank details to complete the check. Once Bajaj Finserv approves, you take the phone and pay monthly. Approval is the lender decision, not the shop.",
  "faq3q": "What is Autopay?",
  "faq3a": "A standing instruction so each EMI is debited on its due date. You choose UPI, card or bank, set a limit, get a reminder before every debit, and can pause or cancel any time.",
  "faq4q": "Can I return what I bought?",
  "faq4a": "Within 7 days of delivery you can ask for a return of a wrong or defective item, with its box and bill. The shop checks it and refunds you. Opened phones are checked by the brand service centre.",
  "faq5q": "How does the warranty work?",
  "faq5a": "Every phone comes with the brand warranty. We record the IMEI on your bill, so your warranty and bill are always in your Orders, even if you lose the paper.",
  "faq6q": "How does delivery work?",
  "faq6a": "Same-day home delivery in town and nearby areas. Elsewhere we send by courier, and phones are prepaid. Cash on delivery is only for local delivery under the shop limit.",
  "faq7q": "What does Reserve mean?",
  "faq7a": "Pay a small token and we hold the phone for you for a few days. Visit the store, pay the rest and take it. If you cancel before the time ends, the token is refunded.",
